Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-05-10
Subject: Make compiler units use compiler-side align helper
License: expat

The i386 backend aligns signed `LongInt` stack sizes.  A bare call binds
to `System.Align(PtrUInt, PtrUInt)` and treats those sizes as addresses.
Import the compiler helper so the operation remains signed `LongInt`
arithmetic.

--- a/compiler/i386/hlcgcpu.pas
+++ b/compiler/i386/hlcgcpu.pas
@@ -53,6 +53,7 @@
   uses
     globals, procinfo, symconst,
     verbose,
+    cutils,
     fmodule,systems,
     aasmbase,aasmtai,aasmcpu,
     paramgr,
